@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Why
+
+Teams are moving to Tidy Tasks from spreadsheets and have many tasks to bring over. Adding them one by one is slow; they need to paste lines of text and have the valid ones added.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `importTasks(list, text)`: one task per line as `title;priority;tags`, priority optional (empty means `normal`), tags separated by spaces. Blank lines are skipped.
+- Every valid line is added to the list; the result is `{ imported, rejected }`, where `rejected` lists `{ line, reason }` for each line that could not be added, `line` counting from 1.
+- Public API: `importTasks` (and its result types) are exported from `src/index.ts`. This is a new export; nothing existing changes.
+
+Project rules touched: TSDoc on every exported function (the new function is documented); errors in the domain (the helper never throws, and reports each failure as a rejected line with the message of the existing error); no clock or randomness (it only calls `list.add`, which owns the clock); no new runtime dependency.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `bulk-task-import`: importing tasks from lines of text, with the lines that could not be added reported.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/domain/import.ts`; `src/index.ts` exports `importTasks` and its types; tests in `test/`.
+- No new dependency, no change to existing behaviour.
